    "done_when": "tests/test_sub_floor_disposition_has_a_writer.py stores a review with one dimension below its floor in a temporary config home, runs the new subcommand through the CLI entry point once with kind folded plus a node id, once with kind exempted plus a reason, asserting after each that the sub-floor obligation row for that dimension is gone on the next obligations read. Four refusal cases (unknown dimension, unknown kind, fold with no node, exemption with no reason) each exit non-zero, name the refusal, leaving the obligation row standing. A further case fails if the shipped default floors in reckon/schema/flight-defaults.yaml are removed. The fold case fails at the base revision because no subcommand exists (logged) and passes at the head. The negative control, in a scratch copy, removes the kind check from dimension_disposition_valid; the unknown-kind refusal case fails, with the mutation on the red log's first line and an EXIT= line after pytest's output. The gate is the new test plus the existing test files that exercise review dispositions or the obligations list; it exits 0, or shows no added failing ids against the base, with both arms recorded as log paths under baseline_suite and after_suite, each ending in an EXIT= line. The test neither reads nor writes the real ~/.config/reckon.",
